{"request_id":"sha256:600fc6e792948b8d5cfdb21dd9322ecabc3a89632846885e5a6af743c9d3b249","units":[{"unit_id":"sha256:b310efaf23ffc795abfa6e1ffd47d0b90d24cdea5182ce7ab1036ff0e9320e8c","reviewed":true,"findings":[{"kind":"AVAILABLE_CAPACITY","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":809}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. states that its in-house manufacturing facility and its partnership with Flex maintained a combined manufacturing capacity of approximately five-million microinverters per quarter, reflecting the domestic manufacturing footprint during fiscal year 2025. This is a quarterly manufacturing capacity figure for microinverters and is not annualized."},{"kind":"CAPACITY_QUALITATIVE","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":834}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. states that it outsources some of its manufacturing to third-party contract manufacturers and believes its contract manufacturing partners have sufficient production capacity to meet anticipated demand for its products for the foreseeable future. This is a qualitative statement about contract manufacturing capacity for the registrant's products and does not provide a comparable actual-output/capacity pair."},{"kind":"SALES_OR_SHIPMENTS","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":804}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. reports that as of December 31, 2025, it has shipped approximately 86.4 million microinverters and more than 5.1 million Enphase residential and commercial systems have been deployed in over 160 countries. These are cumulative shipment and deployment figures, not actual production quantities."},{"kind":"SALES_OR_SHIPMENTS","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":883}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. reports that during the year ended December 31, 2025, it sold approximately 6.4 million microinverter units and shipped 706.1 MWh of IQ Batteries, compared to approximately 6.5 million microinverter units and 521 MWh of IQ Batteries shipped in the year ended December 31, 2024. These are sales and shipment quantities, not actual production amounts."},{"kind":"SALES_OR_SHIPMENTS","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":884}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. reports that net revenues in the United States in the year ended December 31, 2025 included $91.2 million of microinverter shipments associated with safe harbor transactions with customers. This is a shipment-related revenue disclosure, not actual production."},{"kind":"OTHER_CONTEXT","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":806}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. describes fiscal year 2025 priorities including scaling U.S. manufacturing and advancing product qualification to take advantage of the Section 48E investment tax credit and the AMPTC under Section 45X. This is a strategic priority statement and does not provide a production or capacity quantity."},{"kind":"OTHER_CONTEXT","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":818}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. states it has relocated a significant portion of its manufacturing to the United States while continuing to utilize contract manufacturing in China and India, and that certain critical components are still sourced from outside the United States. This is a qualitative operational statement without a production or capacity quantity."},{"kind":"OTHER_CONTEXT","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":819}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. states that LFP battery cells used in its energy storage systems are still supplied exclusively by two vendors located in China and that identifying qualified alternative suppliers with the necessary expertise and capacity remains challenging. This is a supply chain statement about supplier capacity, not the registrant's manufacturing capacity or actual production."},{"kind":"OTHER_CONTEXT","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":830}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. describes cost of revenues components including product costs, warranty, manufacturing and installation services, and states that AMPTC earned under the IRA for U.S. manufactured microinverters shipped to customers are treated as a reduction to cost of revenues. This is a cost accounting description, not a production or capacity quantity."},{"kind":"OTHER_CONTEXT","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":831}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. describes factors impacting product costs such as technological innovations, economies of scale, and improvements in production processes and automation. This is a qualitative cost discussion without a production or capacity quantity."},{"kind":"OTHER_CONTEXT","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":899}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. reports AMPTC benefits recognized of $238.7 million for the year ended December 31, 2025, compared to $157.5 million for the same period in 2024, related to U.S. manufactured microinverters and IQ Batteries MWh shipped to customers. This is a tax credit benefit amount, not a production or capacity quantity."},{"kind":"OTHER_CONTEXT","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":900}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. reports that gross margin included a 16.2 percentage point AMPTC benefit in the year ended December 31, 2025, compared to an 11.8 percentage point AMPTC benefit in the same period in 2024, due to a higher proportion of sales from U.S. manufactured microinverters and IQ Battery MWh shipped. This is a margin impact disclosure, not a production or capacity quantity."},{"kind":"OTHER_CONTEXT","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":986}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. reports open purchase obligations of $252.3 million as of December 31, 2025, related to component inventory that it and its primary contract manufacturers procure on its behalf in accordance with its production forecast. This is a purchase obligation amount, not a production or capacity quantity."},{"kind":"OTHER_CONTEXT","subject":"TARGET_REGISTRANT","timing":"CURRENT_REPORT","evidence":[{"kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":1000}],"reason":"Enphase Energy, Inc. reports that for the year ended December 31, 2025, net cash provided by investing activities included $40.6 million used in purchases of test and assembly equipment for U.S. manufacturing related facility improvements and information technology enhancements. This is a capital expenditure amount, not a production or capacity quantity."}],"unresolved":[]}]}